  "description": "Train movement on the track network (the network counterpart of train-movement.json, ARCHITECTURE decision 51). Nodes 1 (1536, 1536) to 7 (7680, 1536) 1024 units apart, joined by straight edges e1 to e6 of 1024; e7 runs from node 3 south to node 8 (3584, 2560) and, leaving node 3 at a right angle, joins neither e2 nor e3. Every basic step (one second; a minute at normal, two at double) a train travels its share of its rate: to the end of its edge, then into its path, one edge after another. Reaching the end of an edge exactly stops there (offset = length) and does not look at the next entry; a path all entered is stored as [] with cursor 0; with no path a train runs to the end of its edge and stops; an entry it cannot enter (its edge removed) stops it at the end of its edge, the rest of the step's distance unused and the entry kept. setTrainMovementRate and setTrainPath check unknownTrain, trainNotPlaced, then the rate (invalidMovementRate below 0) or the path (invalidContinuation: an edge that does not join at the node ahead, e7 at a right angle, a U-turn back along the train's edge, a gap, or an end at or past the last edge's length, at 0 after an edge, or behind the train on its own edge). Local 1 at 256 along e1 with the path e2, e3: paused, nothing moves; at 1300 a minute it is 532 into e2 (cursor 1), at 124 656, at 1148 780 into e3 (the path all entered), at 244 exactly at the end of e3, where it stays. With the path e4, e5, e6 and e5 removed, it reaches the end of e4 and waits there (cursor 1) while Local 2 runs 512 at 256 a minute to the end of e2; an edge rebuilt from node 5 to node 6 is e8, a new ID, so the old path stays blocked until it is given the path e8, e6. Rate 0 and pause hold it; resumed, it runs on to the end of e6. Local 2, reversed (the end of e2 forward becomes its start backward, the path cleared and the rate kept), runs 1024 in one tick at double, two basic steps, to the end of e2 without entering e1 (cursor 0), then 512 into e1; reversed again (512 back), with no path it runs to the end of e1 and stops, the rest of its distance unused. Unplacing resets its movement. Track costs 1000 per 1024 units of edge; removal is free and not refunded.",
